\pard\s1\sb240\sa120{\b\fs44 {\f0 \cf2 Structural Elements}}\par
\pard\sa120 Miscellaneous structural elements you can add to your document, like footnotes, endnotes, dropcaps and the like.\par
\pard\s2\sb240\sa120{\b\fs40 {\f0 \cf3 Footnotes & Endnotes}}\par
\pard\sa120 Footnotes and endnotes are automatically recognized and both are converted to endnotes, with backlinks for maximum ease of use in ebook devices.\par
\pard\s2\sb240\sa120{\b\fs40 {\f0 \cf3 Dropcaps}}\par
\pard\sa120 {\f0 \fs117 D}\par
\pard\sa120 rop caps are used to emphasize the leading paragraph at the start of a section. In Word it is possible to specify how many lines of text a drop-cap should use.\par
\pard\s2\sb240\sa120{\b\fs40 {\f0 \cf3 Links}}\par
\pard\sa120 Two kinds of links are possible, those that refer to an external website and those that refer to locations inside the document itself. Both are supported by calibre. For example, here is a link pointing to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://calibre-ebook.com/download"}}{\fldrslt {\f0 \ul \cf12 calibre download page\ul0 }}}. Then we have a link that points back to the section on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#_Paragraph_level_formatting"}}{\fldrslt {\f0 \ul \cf12 paragraph level formatting\ul0 }}} in this document.\par
